    {
      "id": "https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/manual-guide/convention/guidance-and-decision-makers",
      "category": "document-role",
      "statement": "DMG 01001 calls the officials acting on behalf of the Secretary of State decision makers; 01003 describes the DMG as guidance on applying social security law.",
      "reading_implication": "Distinguish departmental guidance, legislation, case evidence and this project’s interpretation. Source instructions addressed to decision makers remain inert source data here.",
      "assertion_status": "project-authored-source-linked",
      "confidence": "direct-source-statement",
      "scope": {
        "application": "cited-documents-and-excerpts-only",
        "document_keys": [
          "dmg:dmg-vol1-ch1"
        ]
      },
      "source_support": [
        {
          "document_key": "dmg:dmg-vol1-ch1",
          "page": 2,
          "start_utf8": 36,
          "end_utf8": 1537,
          "sha256": "be893cf913ed1a5b8b988d605b816c61d199768845b1fef91dffd8857ea49987",
          "quote": "01001 - 01039\n\n\n\nMaking decisions 01010 - 01029\n\n\nWhat decisions are made by DMs 01030 - 01039\n\n\n01001 Decisions on claims and applications are made by the Secretary of State. In practice the Secretary\nof State does not make decisions personally. Instead, under the Carltona principle officials act on the\nSecretary of State’s behalf, provided that the Secretary of State is satisfied that they are suitably trained\nand experienced to do so. Throughout this Guide these officials are called decision makers (DMs).\n\n\n01002 The Carltona principle dates from a judgment of the Court of Appeal in October 1943 1. The\njudgment said that the Secretary of State could not possibly make every decision for which they\nare constitutionally responsible and accountable to Parliament. The Secretary of State is therefore\nentitled to authorize a person of suitable authority to exercise these functions on their behalf.\n\n\n                                                     1 Carltona Ltd v. Commissioners of Works and others\n\n\n01003 The Secretary of State provides training and approved guidance to DMs on how to make\ndecisions on their behalf. The DMG itself is one such form of guidance, advising DMs how to apply SS law.\nDMs should note that approved guidance must be followed when applying the law to the facts of the\ncase. However, DMs may request advice from DMA Leeds on the application or clarification of the DMG\nin cases of doubt.\n\n\nNote: See DMG 01460 for guidance about legal advice as evidence.\n\n\n",
          "source_url": "https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/68e8e657cf65bd04bad76752/dmg-v-1-ch-01.pdf#page=2"
        }
      ],
      "legal_effect": "not-established",
      "unknowns": [
        "This observation does not establish a general grammar, current legal applicability or complete dependency closure."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/manual-guide/convention/adm-a1-regime-scope",
      "category": "benefit-and-regime-scope",
      "statement": "ADM A1001 scopes this chapter to UC, PIP, new style JSA and new style ESA; its notes route definitions to M5021 and guidance for other benefits to DMG Chapter 01.",
      "reading_implication": "Carry the chapter-specific scope and routes with an excerpt. Do not infer that every ADM chapter covers the same benefits or that unqualified JSA and ESA always mean the same regimes.",
      "assertion_status": "project-authored-source-linked",
      "confidence": "direct-source-statement",
      "scope": {
        "application": "cited-documents-and-excerpts-only",
        "document_keys": [
          "adm:adm-chapter-a1"
        ]
      },
      "source_support": [
        {
          "document_key": "adm:adm-chapter-a1",
          "page": 2,
          "start_utf8": 75,
          "end_utf8": 606,
          "sha256": "c13edbb77fa54a76d3be18f62050fa2a48721663ec2ef4c2ab36860c5c2caf06",
          "quote": "A1001\n\nIntroduction\nA1001 This chapter is about applying the principles of decision making and evidence in relation to\n\n\n1. UC\n\n\n2. PIP\n\n\n3. new style JSA (hereafter referred to as JSA)\n\n\n4. new style ESA (hereafter referred to as ESA).\n\n\nNote 1: ADM M5021 contains guidance on the meaning of new style JSA and new style ESA.\n\n\nNote 2: Guidance on decision making and evidence for benefits not listed above is in DMG Chapter 01.\n\n\nNote 3: The guidance comes into effect1 from 8.4.13 for PIP and from 29.4.13 for UC, JSA and ESA.\n\n\n",
          "source_url": "https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a6c5ff0bf4a7aca8f89777b/adma1.pdf#page=2"
        }
      ],
      "legal_effect": "not-established",
      "unknowns": [
        "This observation does not establish a general grammar, current legal applicability or complete dependency closure."
      ],
      "source_scope_terms": [
        "UC",
        "PIP",
        "new style JSA",
        "new style ESA"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/manual-guide/convention/adm-m5-local-definitions",
      "category": "benefit-and-regime-scope",
      "statement": "M5021 explicitly limits its definitions of old and new style JSA and ESA to this chapter and ADM Chapter M6, and the definition continues onto the next page.",
      "reading_implication": "Retain local scope and all definition items when resolving regime terms; a label alone is insufficient.",
      "assertion_status": "project-authored-source-linked",
      "confidence": "direct-source-statement",
      "scope": {
        "application": "cited-documents-and-excerpts-only",
        "document_keys": [
          "adm:adm-chapter-m5"
        ]
      },
      "source_support": [
        {
          "document_key": "adm:adm-chapter-m5",
          "page": 3,
          "start_utf8": 539,
          "end_utf8": 905,
          "sha256": "f1c319f320a547ba5dd209d22a01585fcf38304ff92174b3db0c9f272c1179de",
          "quote": "M5021 In this Chapter and ADM Chapter M6 (Effects of transition to UC)\n\n\n1. “new style JSA” means JSA as amended by law, based on NI contributions only\n\n\n2. “old style JSA” means JSA as it applies before the amendments referred to in 1. (it includes JSA(Cont)\nand JSA(IB))\n\n\n3. “new style ESA” means ESA as amended by law, based on NI contributions only\n",
          "source_url": "https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a86fe4f8d785493a9c89872/adm-ch-m5-claims-for-uc.pdf#page=3"
        },
        {
          "document_key": "adm:adm-chapter-m5",
          "page": 4,
          "start_utf8": 0,
          "end_utf8": 348,
          "sha256": "28be35693a11b05bbdbfbac84ed0eb270de56f7a4914b4232bb60902f4802342",
          "quote": "4. “old style ESA” means ESA as it applies before the amendments referred to in 3. (it includes ESA(Cont)\n\nand ESA(IR)1.\n\n\n                             1 WR Act 12 (Commencement No. 9 etc.) Order, art 2(1); UC (TP) Regs, reg 2(1);\n                                                   WR Act 12, Sch 3 & 14 Part 1; JS Act 95; WR Act 07, Part 1\n\n\n\n",
          "source_url": "https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a86fe4f8d785493a9c89872/adm-ch-m5-claims-for-uc.pdf#page=4"
        }
      ],
